Exp-11a :GridLayouts

Aim: To write a Java program to demonstrate GridLayout.

Algorithm:
1. Start the program.
2. Import the AWT package.
3. Create a Frame.
4. Set the layout to GridLayout with 2 rows and 2 columns.
5. Create four buttons.
6. Add the buttons to the frame.
7. Set the size of the frame.
8. Display the frame.
9. Stop the program.

Program:
import java.awt.*;

public class GridLayoutExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Frame f = new Frame("Grid Layout");

        f.setLayout(new GridLayout(2, 2));

        f.add(new Button("Button 1"));
        f.add(new Button("Button 2"));
        f.add(new Button("Button 3"));
        f.add(new Button("Button 4"));

        f.setSize(300, 200);
        f.setVisible(true);
    }
}


Output:









Four buttons are displayed in two rows and two columns with equal sizes.

Result: Thus, the Java program to demonstrate GridLayout was executed successfully.
